    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 passing, including the new `coreComposesSalutation` acceptance test).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: the create-owner request may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner's returned `salutation` is `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nSince owners are created via `POST /api/owners` and read back via a separate `GET /api/owners/{id}`, the title must be persisted so the salutation can be composed on read. I followed the codebase's established pattern for derived fields (each a small pure helper \u2014 `Timezone`, `Locality`, `TelephoneDisplay`, \u2026, delegated to from the MapStruct mapper):\n\n1. **`Salutation.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility helper: `of(title, lastName)` returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or `lastName` alone when the title is null/blank.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter. This lets the existing MapStruct `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` map the incoming title by name automatically (via `BuildOwner`), so no new pipeline step was needed.\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation` mapping delegating to `Salutation.of(owner.getTitle(), owner.getLastName())`, matching the other derived-field mappings.\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` as an optional editable input on `OwnerFields`, and `salutation` as a read-only derived field on `Owner` (these drive the generated DTOs).\n5. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table. The tests run against hsqldb (`ddl-auto=none`, schema-initialized), so this column was required.\n\nNo existing endpoint, controller-equivalent, or logic was touched beyond wiring the new field through the established layers.",
